<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The one-row strip. See prayer_widget_info.xml for why updatePeriodMillis is zero.

    Five cells by one, which on the target device measures 406dp x 96dp — enough for four lines per
    column at legible sizes.

    Both `targetCellWidth`/`targetCellHeight` and `minWidth`/`minHeight` are set, and **they have to
    agree**. The cell counts are honoured from API 31; the dp values size the placement before that,
    and some launchers take the larger of the two either way. The platform derives spans as
    `ceil((size + 30) / 70)`, so those numbers are not free-form:

        5 columns  ->  250 < minWidth  <= 320
        1 row      ->        minHeight <= 40

    A previous minHeight of 90dp derived to two rows and the widget was placed 5x2 despite
    `targetCellHeight="1"`, which is exactly the contradiction this comment exists to prevent.
    Do not raise minHeight to reflect how tall the content is — that is what the row height gives
    you (a 1-row strip measures 96dp on a 450dpi phone), and minResizeHeight is what floors it.

    Vertical resizing is allowed even though the strip is designed for a single row. A launcher
    stores a widget's span when it is placed and does not re-derive it when the app updates, so a
    widget added while the declaration was wrong stays the wrong size forever; without a vertical
    handle the only remedy is to remove and re-add it.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_prayer_strip"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_prayer_strip"
    android:minWidth="320dp"
    android:minHeight="40dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="140dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="50dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="5"
    android:targetCellHeight="1"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:description="@string/strip_widget_description"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0" />
